35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings show that we are spending about 2,300 yen monthly on bathroom spray, often buying duplicates. Also, the management office charges 4,200 yen per hour for professional cleaning.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The timing data shows a full pass takes over an hour. Combined with the previous tenants' note about permanent division leading to conflict, it seems a rigid, long-term split might be counterproductive and underestimated.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we have a fascinating discrepancy. My observations reveal that kitchen usage is heavily skewed toward a few individuals, while our definitions of ""done"" vary wildly, leading to an inconsistent standard of cleanliness.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The bathroom is a disaster waiting to happen; the grout was black again in eleven days! Also, our chat logs prove that most of our fights start with someone nagging another about missed chores. This is exactly why we need a system.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It sounds like we're all seeing different pieces of the same puzzle. I also noticed the previous tenants struggled with conflict, and the calendar shows we're often away, which makes a rigid schedule feel quite risky.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"The duplicate purchases suggest a lack of communication regarding supplies. If we opt for professional cleaning, we must ensure the billing process is transparent to avoid any one person being out of pocket.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, professional cleaning would solve the time issue, but at 4,200 yen per hour, it's a significant cost. We must weigh the financial burden against the risk of burnout and interpersonal conflict.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, a financial cost is far easier to manage than a social one. However, if we simply pay for a service without addressing the skewed usage I observed, we are merely subsidizing the habits of a few.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're being a bit too clinical! Whether one person cooks more or not, we all have to live with the grime. If the bathroom resets to ""gross"" in eleven days, we need a real solution.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I understand your frustration. But @Benjamin is right that we should be fair. Maybe we can find a middle ground that handles the grime without making anyone feel resentful or burdened?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Regardless of who uses the space more, the current supply spending is inefficient. We need a system that tracks both the cleaning tasks and the shared expenses to ensure no one is unfairly burdened financially.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, tracking expenses is logical, but we cannot ignore the time. A full pass takes over an hour; if we rotate, that's a significant block of time. We need a system that minimizes this individual burden.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, while I appreciate the concern for time, we must acknowledge that ""burden"" is subjective. If one person spends an hour cleaning a mess they didn't create, the burden is not just temporal, but psychological.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, stop overthinking the psychology! The psychological burden is me wondering if I'll find mold in the shower today. We need a standard that's actually achievable, or we'll just keep nagging each other.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, I totally get that. It's stressful when you can't relax in your own home. But if we're too strict, we might end up like the previous tenants who stopped speaking. Let's find a gentle way.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"It is clear that we are struggling with both financial inefficiency and inconsistent standards. To avoid the conflicts Midori mentioned, we need a system that is transparent about costs and clear on expectations.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. However, we must ensure the system doesn't create a hidden time tax. If we choose a rotation, we need to be honest about the hour-plus commitment to avoid the resentment the previous tenants faced.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. If we ignore the disparity in usage and the ambiguity of our standards, any system we implement will be a house of cards. We need a solution that balances actual contribution with a unified definition of ""clean.""","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"Look, we can debate the philosophy of fairness all day, but the facts are the facts: the bathroom is a mold trap and we're already fighting. Let's just pick a system that actually works!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree, May. Let's focus on a practical solution. Since we're often away and have different standards, maybe a flexible system or a professional service would keep us all happy and on speaking terms?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
